{"id": "successor-contracts-restart-under-the-line", "title": "In 2026 new agreements again start just under $10 million as the line moves", "seconds": 135.3, "voice": "elevenlabs:OtHu0lbpdNTqJVqaxDtR", "narrator": "Maven", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "8a07b4512b9896b1", "words": 419, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "A City contract needs a Board vote at 10 million dollars. Below that, the department decides.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.86, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "The line", "sub": "$10 million needs a Board vote"}, "emph": ["10 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.3, 0.68, 0.83, 0.9, 1.17, 1.37, 1.49, 1.63, 1.98, 2.54, 2.99, 3.48, 3.56, 3.98]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "amount"], "text": "In 2026, a shelter the Board had already reviewed got a brand new agreement. How far under the line?", "t0": 4.98, "t1": 10.14, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "A new shelter agreement", "sub": "Five Keys, Bayshore Navigation Center"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.27, 0.93, 0.99, 1.26, 1.39, 1.58, 1.66, 1.95, 2.41, 2.63, 2.73, 2.93, 3.07, 3.83, 4.28, 4.46, 4.64, 4.76]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "suspicious[4]"], "text": "18 dollars.", "t0": 10.14, "t1": 11.87, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$18", "label": "under the $10 million line", "sub": "$9,999,982"}, "emph": ["18"], "wt": [0.04, 1.0]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat", "notEstablished[0]"], "text": "It’s a lead, not a finding. No authority has said any amount was picked to dodge a vote.", "t0": 12.39, "t1": 16.92, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.2, 0.82, 0.95, 1.04, 1.68, 1.9, 2.35, 2.49, 2.72, 2.96, 3.22, 3.37, 3.72, 3.9, 4.2, 4.32]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[1]", "story[1]"], "text": "Start with Conard House. It runs three housing hotels.", "t0": 17.14, "t1": 19.8, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Conard House", "sub": "three supportive-housing hotels", "chip": "$7,586,812"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.34, 0.66, 1.11, 1.33, 1.58, 1.78, 2.08]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[1]", "story[1]"], "text": "Its grant began in July 2025 at 7,586,812 dollars.", "t0": 19.92, "t1": 23.81, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Conard House", "sub": "three supportive-housing hotels", "chip": "$7,586,812"}, "emph": ["7,586,812"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.39, 0.66, 0.81, 1.11, 1.32, 1.92, 2.06, 2.3, 2.48, 2.85, 2.99, 3.34]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "In July 2026,", "t0": 23.93, "t1": 25.3, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Conard House", "sub": "first amendment, July 2026", "chip": "$9,997,681"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.37, 0.64]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "the department added five months and 2,410,869 dollars, on its own.", "t0": 25.3, "t1": 29.21, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Conard House", "sub": "first amendment, July 2026", "chip": "$9,997,681"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.13, 0.52, 0.74, 1.0, 1.26, 1.4, 1.64, 1.75, 2.05, 2.21, 2.61, 3.18, 3.27, 3.49]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "The new total? How far under the line?", "t0": 29.33, "t1": 31.69, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Conard House", "sub": "first amendment, July 2026", "chip": "$9,997,681"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.27, 0.82, 1.32, 1.5, 1.68, 1.8]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "2,319 dollars.", "t0": 31.69, "t1": 35.28, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$2,319", "label": "under the line", "sub": "$9,997,681"}, "emph": ["2,319"], "wt": [0.04, 0.89, 1.38, 1.83, 2.32, 3.04]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[1]", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Four months later, it asked the Board for more than three times as much.", "t0": 35.8, "t1": 38.77, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$32,803,756", "label": "adopted by the Board, Nov 3, 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.37, 0.82, 0.9, 1.08, 1.18, 1.48, 1.57, 1.76, 1.9, 2.12, 2.42, 2.53]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[1]", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "On November 3, the Board said yes: 32,803,756 dollars.", "t0": 38.89, "t1": 43.37, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$32,803,756", "label": "adopted by the Board, Nov 3, 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.52, 0.95, 1.04, 1.31, 1.55, 2.24, 2.51, 3.0, 3.36, 3.52, 3.92]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "The first lead: Larkin Street’s youth shelter.", "t0": 43.59, "t1": 46.32, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Larkin Street, Lark Inn shelter", "rows": [["first", "7193184"], ["May 2025", "9440036"], ["July 2026", "9915387"], ["to the Board", "14926904"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.43, 0.97, 1.42, 1.83, 2.16]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "Raised twice with no vote,", "t0": 46.44, "t1": 48.05, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Larkin Street, Lark Inn shelter", "rows": [["first", "7193184"], ["May 2025", "9440036"], ["July 2026", "9915387"], ["to the Board", "14926904"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.56, 0.73, 0.93]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "to 9,440,036,", "t0": 48.05, "t1": 49.7, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Larkin Street, Lark Inn shelter", "rows": [["first", "7193184"], ["May 2025", "9440036"], ["July 2026", "9915387"], ["to the Board", "14926904"]]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.16, 0.38, 0.64, 0.92, 1.18]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "then 9,915,387 dollars.", "t0": 49.7, "t1": 52.11, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Larkin Street, Lark Inn shelter", "rows": [["first", "7193184"], ["May 2025", "9440036"], ["July 2026", "9915387"], ["to the Board", "14926904"]]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.45, 0.67, 0.92, 1.21, 1.51, 1.81]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "established[2]"], "text": "Then 14,926,904 went to the Board, whose record lists it as passed.", "t0": 52.23, "t1": 56.38, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "unresolved invoicing findings"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.31, 0.67, 0.97, 1.12, 1.45, 1.63, 1.69, 1.81, 2.51, 2.72, 3.0, 3.3, 3.41, 3.62]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[9]", "established[3]"], "text": "The department says that extension, to June 2029, fits its plan to rebid everything.", "t0": 56.5, "t1": 61.57, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$25,737,447", "label": "Bayview Hunters Point Foundation, from $9,989,926"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.52, 0.75, 0.86, 1.56, 1.65, 1.91, 2.17, 2.97, 3.43, 3.6, 3.89, 4.0, 4.45]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[4]"], "text": "The second lead moved in round steps.", "t0": 61.79, "t1": 63.78, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Urban Alchemy, street response", "rows": [["May 2023", "2750000"], ["March 2024", "4490000"], ["July 2024", "9000000"], ["July 2026", "9900000"]]}, "wt": [0.02, 0.07, 0.36, 0.68, 0.94, 1.08, 1.39]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[4]"], "text": "Urban Alchemy’s street team contract went to exactly 9 million. Then to exactly 9.9 million.", "t0": 63.9, "t1": 69.55, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Urban Alchemy, street response", "rows": [["May 2023", "2750000"], ["March 2024", "4490000"], ["July 2024", "9000000"], ["July 2026", "9900000"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.61, 0.82, 1.04, 1.54, 1.69, 1.83, 2.22, 2.44, 3.2, 3.83, 3.97, 4.42, 4.64, 4.94, 5.11]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[4]", "story[2]"], "text": "Only then did it go to the Board, for 14,630,871 dollars.", "t0": 69.67, "t1": 73.88, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$14,630,871", "label": "Amendment No. 5, pending"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 0.58, 0.76, 0.84, 0.96, 1.02, 1.13, 1.88, 1.99, 2.31, 2.71, 3.0, 3.24, 3.59]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[4]", "story[2]"], "text": "It’s pending.", "t0": 74.0, "t1": 74.53, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$14,630,871", "label": "Amendment No. 5, pending"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[5]"], "text": "The third lead is a matching number. Two different groups got housing-subsidy agreements in July 2026.", "t0": 74.75, "t1": 80.85, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Brilliant Corners", "$9,946,798"], "b": ["Compass Family Services", "$9,946,798"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.36, 0.64, 0.81, 0.88, 1.22, 1.84, 2.47, 2.81, 3.09, 3.28, 4.02, 4.48, 4.64, 4.94, 5.21]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[5]"], "text": "Same amount to the dollar: 9,946,798.", "t0": 80.97, "t1": 83.61, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Brilliant Corners", "$9,946,798"], "b": ["Compass Family Services", "$9,946,798"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.39, 0.47, 0.61, 1.27, 1.48, 1.69, 2.0, 2.16]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "That suggests the department set the number, not each group’s budget.", "t0": 83.73, "t1": 86.69, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "set by the department rather than built from each provider’s budget"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.46, 0.55, 1.03, 1.19, 1.29, 1.94, 2.08, 2.28, 2.57]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[6]"], "text": "The fourth lead: shelters the Board already reviewed, signed again just under the line.", "t0": 86.91, "t1": 90.92, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Board approved before", "$25,071,113"], "b": ["new agreement", "$9,999,982"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.34, 0.73, 1.22, 1.3, 1.5, 1.79, 2.36, 2.81, 3.08, 3.27, 3.47, 3.62]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[6]"], "text": "Bayshore: the Board approved 25,071,113 before. Now?", "t0": 91.04, "t1": 95.44, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Board approved before", "$25,071,113"], "b": ["new agreement", "$9,999,982"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.7, 0.94, 1.15, 1.54, 1.74, 2.24, 2.59, 2.68, 3.04, 3.64]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[6]"], "text": "9,999,982 dollars.", "t0": 95.44, "t1": 96.92, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$9,999,982", "label": "Five Keys, Bayshore, two years"}, "emph": ["9,999,982"], "wt": [0.04, 0.44, 0.67, 0.96]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["established[6]", "suspicious[4].why"], "text": "711 Post: 9,847,270.", "t0": 97.44, "t1": 100.65, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Re-signed under the line", "rows": [["260 Golden Gate", "9997940"], ["711 Post", "9847270"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.45, 0.83, 1.64, 1.91, 2.12, 2.42, 2.61]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["established[6]", "suspicious[4].why"], "text": "All were once under Board review.", "t0": 100.77, "t1": 102.37, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Re-signed under the line", "rows": [["260 Golden Gate", "9997940"], ["711 Post", "9847270"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.51, 0.7, 0.91, 1.19]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["notEstablished[1]"], "text": "At Bayshore’s old rate, 4.56 million a year, two years comes to about 9.1 million.", "t0": 102.49, "t1": 107.52, "shot": "b17a", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$9.1 million", "label": "two years at Bayshore’s earlier rate of $4.56 million a year"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.49, 0.69, 1.0, 1.16, 1.46, 1.64, 1.87, 2.17, 2.29, 2.94, 3.08, 3.35, 3.59, 3.67, 3.88, 4.09, 4.39, 4.49]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[4]", "established[7]"], "text": "Then the line itself moved.", "t0": 107.74, "t1": 108.97, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Proposition E", "kicker": "The line moves", "sub": "approved Nov 3, 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.2, 0.42, 0.82]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[4]", "established[7]"], "text": "On November 3, 2026, voters passed Proposition E. Where is the line now?", "t0": 109.09, "t1": 114.31, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Proposition E", "kicker": "The line moves", "sub": "approved Nov 3, 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.42, 0.74, 0.95, 1.65, 2.15, 2.42, 3.04, 3.53, 4.35, 4.46, 4.56, 4.84]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[7]"], "text": "25 million dollars.", "t0": 114.31, "t1": 116.63, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$25 million", "label": "the new Board-approval line"}, "emph": ["25"], "wt": [0.04, 1.27, 1.69]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[7]", "established[8]"], "text": "In June 2026, a grand jury warned that renewals slip under review.", "t0": 117.15, "t1": 120.73, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "no additional review for contracts between $10 million and $25 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.35, 0.61, 1.31, 1.41, 1.63, 1.88, 2.12, 2.22, 2.68, 2.87, 3.1]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[4]"], "text": "The records don’t show the new deals will pass 10 million. Or that any provider overbilled.", "t0": 120.95, "t1": 125.77, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That the new agreements will pass $10 million", "That any provider overbilled"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.41, 0.6, 0.9, 1.03, 1.17, 1.42, 1.58, 1.83, 1.98, 2.73, 3.42, 3.56, 3.71, 4.12]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? The budgets behind each number, and what the department expected to spend.", "t0": 125.89, "t1": 129.96, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The budgets behind $9,999,982, $9,997,940 and $9,946,798"}, {"who": "", "what": "The department’s spending forecast for each site"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.2, 0.55, 0.77, 0.91, 1.3, 1.63, 1.83, 2.27, 2.36, 2.54, 2.63, 3.03, 3.43, 3.59]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "No authority has examined the sizing.", "t0": 130.08, "t1": 131.84, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.54, 0.73, 1.04, 1.17]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 131.96, "t1": 134.41, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.36, 0.49, 0.57, 1.38, 1.63, 1.78]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "found": "On the record", "lead1": "Lead 1 · raised twice, no vote", "lead2": "Lead 2 · round steps", "lead3": "Lead 3 · the same amount", "lead4": "Lead 4 · re-signed under", "lead5": "Lead 5 · the line moves", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "newsroom", "hook": "timeline"}